TEXT -96 752 Left 2 !.tran 10n 60u
TEXT -96 904 Left 2 ;Low-dropout regulator from 3.3 V to 1.2 V on IHP's 3.3 V devices. The error amplifier compares out with the 1.2 V reference\n(feed ref from a bandgap) and drives the gate of the PMOS pass device MP, so out follows ref (unity feedback; add a divider\nfor a higher output). The load steps from 0.1 mA to 10 mA at 20 us and back at 40 us into 1 uF with 0.2 ohm ESR, whose zero keeps\nthe loop stable. Between the loads out moves by about Iload / (gm(MP) A), A the amplifier gain; a wider MP lowers the dropout and the droop.
